{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-183764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S={...,-4,-2,0,2,4,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=2$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\n2n+1\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,-4,\\,-2,\\,0,\\,2,\\,4,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =-2-(-4) \\\\  & =0-(-2) \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=2,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =2+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={2n\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183764" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-183764" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183764" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2n"] ["math" "2n+1"] ["math" "2n+3"] ["math" "n"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183764" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2n"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183764" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183764" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\in N"] ["math" "\\in Q"] ["math" "\\in Z"] ["math" "\\text{is even}"] ["math" "\\text{is odd}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183764" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\in Z"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S={...,-21,-17,-13,-9,-5,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=-5$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\n4n-9\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,-21,\\,-17,\\,-13,\\,-9,\\,-5,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =4 \\\\  & =-17-(-21) \\\\  & =-13-(-17) \\\\  & =-9-(-13) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=-5,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =-5+(n-1)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={4n-9\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-183770" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183770" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2n-1"] ["math" "4n+21"] ["math" "4n-9"] ["math" "7n"] ["math" "n+4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183770" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type