value" [:answer.type/math "\\in Z"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S={...,-24,-19,-14,-9,-4,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take ${a}_{1}=-4$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*\n\n$$\n5n+2\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n…,\\,-24,\\,-19,\\,-14,\\,-9,\\,-4,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =5 \\\\  & =-19-(-24) \\\\  & =-14-(-19) \\\\  & =-9-(-14) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=-4,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =-4+(n-1)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-4+5n-5 \\\\  & =5n-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={5n-9\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-183766" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "cat