et\n\n$$\n…,\\,-2,\\,4,\\,-8,\\,16,\\,-32,\\,…\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =-2 \\\\  & =(\\frac{4}{-2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-8}{4}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{16}{-8}) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  ${a}_{1}=-2,$ the $n$th term ${a}_{n}$ of our sequence for $n\\in Z$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-2)^{n-1} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-2)^{n}\\cdot (-2)^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{-2}\\cdot (-2)^{n} \\\\  & =(-2)^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS={(-2)^{n}\\,:\\,n\\in Z}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183771" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-183771" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183771" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2)^{n}"] ["math" "-1\\cdot {2}^{n}"] ["math" "{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}"] ["math" "{2}^{n}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183771" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-2)^{n}"] "category" "model_in