$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $S$ contains all natural numbers greater than or equal to $5.$\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x\\ge 5}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example:\n\n- We can write $x\\in Z.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:x\\ge 5}.\n$$\n\n- We can write $x>4.$ This gives\n\n$$\nS={x\\in N\\,:\\,x>4},\n$$\n\nor, writing $x\\in Z$ as before, we have\n\n$$\nS={x\\in Z\\,:\\,x>4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183663" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-183663" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183663" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "C"] ["math" "N"] ["math" "Q"] ["math" "R"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183663" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "N"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183663" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183663" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183663" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-1,\\frac{1}{3}}$ given below.\n\n${-1,\\frac{1}{3}}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,3{q}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n$q\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given set contains the roots $q\\in Q$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(q).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${q}_{1}=-1$ and ${q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(q) & =a(q-{q}_{1})(q-{q}_{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (q-(-1))(q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3(q+1)(q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3({q}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}q-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =3{q}^{2}+2q-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-1,\\frac{1}{3}}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,3{q}^{2}+2q-1=0}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-181695" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181695" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181695" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181695" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-\\frac{1}{2},3}$ given below.\n\n${-\\frac{1}{2},3}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,4{q}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$q\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given set contains the roots $q\\in Q$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(q).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${q}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${q}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(q) & =a(q-{q}_{1})(q-{q}_{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (q-(-\\frac{1}{2}))(q-3) \\\\  & =4(q+\\frac{1}{2})(q-3) \\\\  & =4({q}^{2}-\\frac{5q}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =4{q}^{2}-10q-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{-\\frac{1}{2},3}={q\\in Q\\,:\\,4{q}^{2}-10q-6=0}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183704" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-183704" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183704" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183704" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183704" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}$ given below.\n\n${-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}\n${x}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some cubic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{2}=-\\sqrt{5},$ and ${x}_{3}=\\sqrt{5},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(3)(x-(-3))(x-(-\\sqrt{5}))(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x+\\sqrt{5})(x-\\sqrt{5}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-\\sqrt{5}x+\\sqrt{5}x-(\\sqrt{5})^{2}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)({x}^{2}-5) \\\\  & =3({x}^{3}-5x+3{x}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as\n\n$$\n{-3,-\\sqrt{5},\\sqrt{5}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}-15x-45=0}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183751" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "45"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${1\\pm \\text{i}}$ given below.\n\n${1\\pm \\text{i}}={z\\in C\\,:\\,2{z}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$z\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given set contains the roots $z\\in C$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(z).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=1-\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=1+\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (z-(1-\\text{i}))(z-(1+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(1-\\text{i})z-(1+\\text{i})z+(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(1-\\text{i}+1+\\text{i})z+((1)^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(2)z+(1+1)) \\\\  & =2{z}^{2}-4z+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{1\\pm \\text{i}}={z\\in C\\,:\\,2{z}^{2}-4z+4=0}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-183730" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183730" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183730" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-183730" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${3,4}$ given below.\n\n${3,4}={n\\in Z\\,:\\,2{n}^{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$n\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$=0}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given set contains the roots $n\\in Z$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(n).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${n}_{1}=3$ and ${n}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(n) & =a(n-{n}_{1})(n-{n}_{2}) \\\\  & =2(n-3)(n-4) \\\\  & =2({n}^{2}-7n+12) \\\\  & =2{n}^{2}-14n+24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{3,4}={n\\in Z\\,:\\,2{n}^{2}-14n+24=0}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fc2548584afdb3016c6caf43bf436c68ea1ae5b5f9e2fdb262895e441a976cbc"} {"question" "q-181608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181608" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "q-181608" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/state.json" "file_sha256" "792966511c878b86a039ac7de776761cc4b5ff959d6c68585ce77cf462836283"} {"question" "e-13186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S=\\{... , -5, -3, -1, 1, 3, ...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_1 = 1$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13186.json" "file_sha256" "4e28a5a983680d8835a838216b2c38bb985188b593a2bc0268a30289396271d9"} {"question" "e-13186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\\ldots, \\quad -5, \\quad -3, \\quad -1, \\quad 1, \\quad 3, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =2 \\\\  & =-3-(-5) \\\\  & =-1-(-3) \\\\  & =1-(-1) \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  $a_1=1,$ the $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)\\cdot d \\\\  & =1+(n-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1+2n-2 \\\\  & =2n-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{2n-1 \\: : \\: n \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\big\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!** \n\nThe constructive definition of a set is typically not unique. \n\nSince the elements of $A$ are generated by a *two-way* infinite arithmetic sequence, we could have picked *any* term in our sequence as $a_1$ when determining $a_n.$ We selected $a_1 = 1$ because this led to a nice, simple expression in our constructive definition." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13186.json" "file_sha256" "4e28a5a983680d8835a838216b2c38bb985188b593a2bc0268a30289396271d9"} {"question" "e-13184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S=\\left\\{\\ldots, -36, -6, -1, -\\dfrac1{6}, -\\dfrac1{36}, ...\\right\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_1 = -\\dfrac16$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13184.json" "file_sha256" "72d30fe7f318869c172c91967ff9aa4f36e03b275e755780e3f82939c96f026c"} {"question" "e-13184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\\ldots,\\quad -36, \\quad -6, \\quad -1, \\quad -\\dfrac1{6}, \\quad -\\dfrac1{36}, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio $r=\\dfrac16{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =(\\frac{-6}{-36}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-1}{-6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{6})}{(-1)} \\\\  & =⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting  $a_1=-\\dfrac16,$ the $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{6})\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n-1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{6})\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{-1}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n} \\\\  & =-{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\left\\{-\\left(\\dfrac16\\right)^{n} \\: : \\: n\\in \\mathbb{Z}\\right\\}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13184.json" "file_sha256" "72d30fe7f318869c172c91967ff9aa4f36e03b275e755780e3f82939c96f026c"} {"question" "e-13144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Describe the set $S = \\{-9,-8,-7, ..., 5\\}$ using a conditional definition." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13144.json" "file_sha256" "f9bca9264e33226bba8d40c4e5c433d6162b3d86ef2d8894821c12bf1df6e663"} {"question" "e-13144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-9$ and $5$ (including $-9$ and $5$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS = \\{ x \\in \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\mathbb Z} \\: : \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-9} \\leq x \\leq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5} \\}.\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example, we can write $S$ equivalently as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{ x \\in \\mathbb Z \\: : \\: -10 \\lt x \\lt 6 \\big\\}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13144.json" "file_sha256" "f9bca9264e33226bba8d40c4e5c433d6162b3d86ef2d8894821c12bf1df6e663"} {"question" "e-13185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the missing coefficients $p$ and $q$ in the conditional definition of the set given below.\n\n$$\n\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\: : \\: 4z^2+pz+q = 0 \\Big\\}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13185.json" "file_sha256" "e31073c8c1948cad40bb127a3a64a0f40b2aed3a713ab0c190e95d65180c2a2d"} {"question" "e-13185" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given set contains the roots $z\\in\\mathbb C$ of some quadratic polynomial $f(z).$\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots $z_1=-3\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (z-(-3\\text{i}))(z-(3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot (z+3\\text{i})(z-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}-9{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot ({z}^{2}+9) \\\\  & =4{z}^{2}+36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\: : \\: 4z^2+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}z+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}36} = 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=0$ and $q=36.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040040/example-13185.json" "file_sha256" "e31073c8c1948cad40bb127a3a64a0f40b2aed3a713ab0c190e95d65180c2a2d"}] "usage" {"q-181695" [] "e-13186" [] "e-13184" [] "q-181608" [] "q-183328" [] "e-13185" [] "q-183764" [] "e-13144" []} "basis" 1407 "retractions" [[17592186198799 :question/problem "Describe the set $S = {...,-4,-2, 0, 2, 4,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_{1} = 2$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S$.*\n\n$2n$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}"] [17592186198799 :question/answer-fields 17592186196323] [17592186198771 :question/problem "Describe the set $S = {…, 3, 6, 12, 24, 48,...}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_{1} = 6$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S$.*\n\n$2^{n}$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}"] [17592186198771 :question/answer-fields 17592186195938] [17592186198721 :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the constructive definition of the set ${-1, \\frac{1}{3}}$ given below.${-1, \\frac{1}{3}} = {q ∈ Q: 3q^{2} +$\n{{field-1}}\n$q -$\n{{field-2}}\n$= 0}$"] [17592186198716 :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the constructive definition of the set ${3, 4}$ given below.${3, 4} = {n ∈ Z: 2n^{2} -$\n{{field-1}}\n$n +$\n{{field-2}}\n$= 0}$"] [17592186198094 :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\{..., -5, -3, -1, 1, 3,...\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_1 = 1$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S$.*"] [17592186198094 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n$\\ldots, \\quad -5, \\quad -3, \\quad -1, \\quad 1, \\quad 3, \\quad \\ldots$\nform a two-way infinite arithmetic sequence with common difference $d=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= 2 \\\\\n&=-3 - (-5) \\\\\n&=-1 - (-3) \\\\\n&= 1 - (-1) \\\\\n&= ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $a_1=1$, the $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} + (n - 1) \\cdot d \\\\\n&= 1 + (n - 1) \\cdot 2 \\\\\n&= 1 + 2n - 2 \\\\\n&= 2n - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{2n-1 \\:: \\: n \\in \\mathbb{Z}\\big\\}\n$$\n\n**Watch Out!**\n\nThe constructive definition of a set is typically not unique.\n\nSince the elements of $A$ are generated by a *two-way* infinite arithmetic sequence, we could have picked *any* term in our sequence as $a_1$ when determining $a_n$. We selected $a_1 = 1$ because this led to a nice, simple expression in our constructive definition."] [17592186198092 :question/problem "Describe the set $S=\\left\\{\\ldots, -36, -6, -1, -\\dfrac1{6}, -\\dfrac1{36},...\\right\\}$ using a constructive definition.\n\n*Hint: Take $a_1 = -\\dfrac16$ in the sequence that generates the elements of $S$.*"] [17592186198092 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the elements of our set\n\n$$\n\\ldots,\\quad -36, \\quad -6, \\quad -1, \\quad -\\dfrac1{6}, \\quad -\\dfrac1{36}, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nform a two-way infinite geometric sequence with a common ratio\n\n$$\nr=\\dfrac16{:}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= \\frac{1}{6} \\\\\n&= (\\frac{-6}{-36}) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{-1}{-6}) \\\\\n&= ((-\\frac{1}{6}))/((-1)) \\\\\n&= ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting\n\n$$\na_1=-\\dfrac16\n$$\n\nthe $n$th term $a_n$ of our sequence for $n\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} \\cdot r^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= (-\\frac{1}{6}) \\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})^{n - 1} \\\\\n&= - (\\frac{1}{6}) \\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})^{-1} \\cdot (\\frac{1}{6})^{n} \\\\\n&= - (\\frac{1}{6})^{n}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can define our set using a constructive definition as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\left\\{-\\left(\\dfrac16\\right)^{n} \\:: \\: n\\in \\mathbb{Z}\\right\\}\n$$"] [17592186198078 :question/problem "Describe the set $S = \\{-9,-8,-7,..., 5\\}$ using a conditional definition."] [17592186198078 :question/worked-solution "The set $S$ contains all integer numbers between $-9$ and $5$ (including $-9$ and $5$).\n\nTherefore, the set can be written as\n\n$$\nS = \\{x \\in \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\mathbb Z} \\:: \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-9} \\leq x \\leq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}5} \\}\n$$\n\n**Note**: This definition is not unique. For example, we can write $S$ equivalently as follows:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{x \\in \\mathbb Z \\:: \\: -10 \\lt x \\lt 6 \\big\\}\n$$"] [17592186198093 :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients $p$ and $q$ in the constructive definition of the set given below.\n\n$\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\:: \\: 4z^2+pz+q = 0 \\Big\\}$"] [17592186198093 :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $z\\in\\mathbb C$ of some quadratic polynomial $f(z)$.\n\nSince the quadratic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\nz_1=-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nz_2=3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4$, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(z) &= a(z - z_{1})(z - z_{2}) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot (z - (-3\\textrm{i}))(z - (3\\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot (z + 3\\textrm{i})(z - 3\\textrm{i}) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot (z^{2} - (3\\textrm{i})^{2}) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot (z^{2} - 9\\textrm{i}^{2}) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot (z^{2} + 9) \\\\\n&= 4z^{2} + 36\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\pm 3\\textrm{i}\\} = \\Big\\{z \\in \\mathbb{C} \\:: \\: 4z^2+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0}z+\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}36} = 0 \\Big\\}\n$$\n\nFinally, $p=0$ and $q=36$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186195939 17592186195940 17592186195941 17592186195942 17592186195943 17592186195945 17592186195946 17592186195947 17592186196319 17592186196320 17592186196321 17592186196322 17592186196324 17592186196325 17592186196326 17592186196327 17592186196328] "immutable_fields" [[17592186195307 :answer-field/id] [17592186195307 :answer-field/key] [17592186195307 :answer-field/type] [17592186195308 :answer-field/id] [17592186195308 :answer-field/key] [17592186195308 :answer-field/type] [17592186195342 :answer-field/id] [17592186195342 :answer-field/key] [17592186195342 :answer-field/type] [17592186195343 :answer-field/id] [17592186195343 :answer-field/key] [17592186195343 :answer-field/type] [17592186195938 :answer-field/id] [17592186195938 :answer-field/key] [17592186195938 :answer-field/type] [17592186195944 :answer-field/id] [17592186195944 :answer-field/key] [17592186195944 :answer-field/type] [17592186196318 :answer-field/id] [17592186196318 :answer-field/key] [17592186196318 :answer-field/type] [17592186196323 :answer-field/id] [17592186196323 :answer-field/key] [17592186196323 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
